findings.body:
**Replace the `effects` spread with explicit delegation.**

`ReviewLaunchEffects` is an interface of methods, so a class instance satisfies the `effects` parameter of `QueueCell.launch`. The spread at `src/queue-runner/queueCell.ts:213` copies only own enumerable properties. Prototype methods such as `writeMeta` are not copied. `reserveAndSpawnReview` then calls `effects.writeMeta(...)` at `src/queue-runner/reviewLaunch.ts:98`, which can throw a `TypeError` for such an instance. Delegating each member explicitly keeps the original `effects` receiver for every call.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
     const saving: ReviewLaunchEffects = {
-      ...effects,
+      writeMeta: (runId, meta) => effects.writeMeta(runId, meta),
+      workStarted: (meta) => effects.workStarted(meta),
+      spawn: (runId) => effects.spawn(runId),
+      event: (kind, data) => effects.event(kind, data),
+      nowIso: () => effects.nowIso(),
       saveQueue: async (queue) => {
         await effects.saveQueue(queue);
         lastSaved = queue;
       },
     };
```

</details>
